       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/al-wadi-al-gadid",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000000b",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "The Dawn of the Temples"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "h3"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000013",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000c",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Initiated in 1244 BC, the construction of the "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000000d"
       ],
       "text": "Abu Simbel"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000000f",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " temple complex was an ambitious project that spanned two decades. These temples, carved into the heart of the mountain, emerged as a symbol of Pharaonic power and architectural prowess. Built during the reign of Ramses II, they served a dual purpose: demonstrating the might of a powerful king to the Nubians and honoring Ramses II’s divine stature as the beloved of Amun, the king of gods. This construction was part of a series of six grand rock-cut temples in Nubia, each a testament to Ramses II’s rule and "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000011",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000010"
       ],
       "text": "Egypt’s"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000012",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " architectural zenith during the New Kingdom."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "00000000000d",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/abu-simble-travel-guide/qasr-ibrim/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/abu-simbel/qasr-ibrim",
       "newTab": false
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000010",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/contact-us/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/contact",
       "newTab": false
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000014",
     "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Abu-Simble-front-scene.jpg",
     "_type": "image",
     "alt": [
      {
       "_key": "en",
       "value": "Partial view of the Abu Simbel temple with its colossal statues partly in ruins."
      }
     ],
     "caption": [
      {
       "_key": "en",
       "value": "Time-worn statues of Abu Simbel stand tall against the elements."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000016",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000015",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Rediscovery Under the Sands"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "h3"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000021",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000017",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Over centuries, the shifting sands of Nubia buried these architectural wonders, obscuring them from the world. It wasn’t until 1813 that a Swiss orientalist pinpointed the temple’s location, leading to their excavation. In 1817, Italian "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000019",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000018"
       ],
       "text": "explorer"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " Giovanni Battista Belzoni played a pivotal role in unearthing and accessing the temples. Entwined with these historical facts are local legends, often recounted by Egyptian "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001c",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000001b"
       ],
       "text": "tour"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001d",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " guides, suggesting that the complex was named after a young boy, Abu Simbel, who guided archaeologists to the site. Alternatively, some records indicate that the temples took their name from the nearby "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000001f",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000001e"
       ],
       "text": "village of Abu Simbel"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000020",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000018",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/nuweiba-travel-guide/exploring/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/guide/nuweiba",
       "newTab": false
      },
