       "_key": "en",
       "value": "The towering legacy of Ramses II at Abu Simbel, seen from below."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000024",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000023",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "The Monumental Relocation"
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "h3"
    },
    {
     "_key": "00000000002f",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000025",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "The construction of the High Dam in "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000027",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000026"
       ],
       "text": "Aswan"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000028",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " in the mid-20th century posed an existential threat to the Abu Simbel temples. Submerged under the waters of "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002a",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "000000000029"
       ],
       "text": "Lake Nasser"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002b",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": ", these ancient marvels faced oblivion. This dire circumstance prompted "
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002d",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [
        "00000000002c"
       ],
       "text": "UNESCO,"
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002e",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " in 1960, to issue a global appeal to save the Nubian monuments, including Abu Simbel. An international collaboration ensued, involving over 50 nations, including the United States, the Netherlands, Great Britain, Spain, and many others, alongside the Egyptian government and UNESCO."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000026",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/about-egypt/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/travel-tips/about-egypt",
       "newTab": false
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000029",
       "_pendingInternalRef": {
        "sourceLocale": "en",
        "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/lake-nasser-cruises/"
       },
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "/blog/lake-nasser-cruise",
       "newTab": false
      },
      {
       "_key": "00000000002c",
       "_type": "externalLink",
       "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO",
       "newTab": true
      }
     ],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000031",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000030",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "This rescue mission entailed slicing the larger temple of Ramses II into approximately 830 blocks and the smaller temple of Queen Nefertari into 235 blocks, each weighing around 20 tons. This intricate process was part of one of the 20th century’s most astounding architectural feats. In 1965, these pieces were meticulously moved to a new location, elevated over 150 meters above sea level to safeguard them against future Nile floods."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000033",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000032",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Behind these relocated temples, engineers constructed an artificial mountain, forming a dome between 60 to 65 meters in diameter and 38 meters high, to replicate the original rock-cut ambiance. This reconstruction, completed in 1968, spanned four years and cost around 36 million US dollars, underscoring the global commitment to preserving this irreplaceable piece of ancient Egyptian heritage."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000038",
     "_type": "block",
     "children": [
      {
       "_key": "000000000034",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Today, the "
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000036",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": "Abu Simbel temples"
      },
      {
       "_key": "000000000037",
       "_type": "span",
       "marks": [],
       "text": " stand not just as monuments of ancient grandeur but also as symbols of international cooperation and the enduring power of human ingenuity."
      }
     ],
     "markDefs": [],
     "style": "normal"
    },
    {
     "_key": "000000000039",
     "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/abusimbel6.jpg",
     "_type": "image",
     "alt": [
      {
